//     with the repo'''s own parameters via scipy.integrate.solve_ivp; heatmap
//     grids are downsampled from the original resolution for bundle size, same
//     deterministic model, just fewer sample points.
//   - Genome-scale FBA models (yeast/bacillus-aerobic-anaerobic, cyano-*):
//     github.com/Halion1/iGEM-KAUST-Drylab (obj2_gem/) notebooks. The two
//     aerobic/anaerobic bars are the exact cached slim_optimize() values from
//     the notebooks''' own saved output. The 5 cyanobacteria sweeps were
//     re-run with cobrapy against the public iMS837 model (github.com/MariaS87/
//     GEM-Synechococcus-elongatus-PCC-7942-iMS837) -- the repo'''s copy had
//     EX_so4_e capped at (-0.03, 1000) where the notebook'''s own cached
//     printout documents the model'''s real default as (-1000, 1000)
//     (sulfate unconstrained); with that one bound restored, every cached
//     checkpoint in the notebook (baseline growth, all four figure anchor
//     points) reproduces to 4+ decimal places.
//   - Oxygen/viability FBA sweeps (yeast/bacillus/pichia-o2-sweep,
